      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 22-yr-old man was found to have a subtotally occluding thrombus in the proximal left anterior descending (LAD) coronary artery shortly after suffering mild blunt chest trauma. After 6 days of anticoagulant therapy, the LAD appeared angiographically normal."},
